","(a) The integral of $2^x$ is $\frac{e^x}{\ln 2}$.  
$$
\int_{-1}^{1} 2^{x} d x = \frac{e^x}{\ln 2}|_{_{-1}^{1}} = \frac{e^1}{\ln 2} - \frac{e^{-1}}{\ln 2} = \frac{e - \frac{1}{e}}{\ln 2} = \frac{e^2 - 1}{e \ln 2}.
$$  
(b) The integral of $3e^x + 2\sqrt{x}$ is $3e^x + 2 \cdot \frac{2}{3} x^{3/2}$.  
$$
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = 3e^x + \frac{4}{3} x^{3/2}|_{_{0}^{1}} = \left(3e^1 + \frac{4}{3} (1)^{3/2}\right) - \left(3e^0 + \frac{4}{3} (0)^{3/2}\right) = 3e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 = 3e - \frac{5}{3}.
$$  
(c) The integral of $2^{2 y}$ is $\frac{e^{2y}}{\ln 2}$.  
\[
\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y = \frac{e^{2y}}{\ln 2}|_{_{0}^{1}} = \frac{e^{2 \cdot 1}}{\ln 2} - \frac{e^{2 \cdot 0}}{\ln 2} = \frac{e^2 - 1}{\ln 2}.
\]  

