\]
Since \( p^2 \geq 0 \) for all \( p \), the only way for the sum of \( p^2 \cdot \mathcal{P}(X = p) \) to be zero is if each term in the sum is zero. Thus, \( p^2 \cdot \mathcal{P}(X = p) = 0 \) for all \( p \).

