","To calculate the average radiation dose to the liver, we use the formula:  
\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = \0.01 \times \frac{\text{absorbed dose (mSv)}}{\text{mass (g)}}
\]  
Given:  
- Absorbed dose = 0.12 J  
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg = 1.6000 kg = 1,600 g  

First, convert the absorbed dose from joules to millisieverts (mSv). The conversion factor is 1 J = 1 mSv/g.  
\[
\text{Absoseed dose (mSv)} = 0.12 \text{ J} \times 1000 \text{ J/kg} = 120 \text{ mSv}
\]  
Now, calculate the dose:  
\[
\text{dose (mSv)} = 0.01 \times \frac{120 \text{ mSv}}{1,600 \text{ g}} = 0.075 \text{ mSv/g}
\]  
Thus, the average radiation dose to the liver is \(\boxed{0.075 \text{ mSv/g}}\).",fluency,"# Task Description
