","The differential cross-section for elastic scattering is given by:
\[
\frac{d\sigma}{d\Omega} = \frac{4\pi}{2m_e} \frac{d\sigma}{d\Omega} \approx \frac{2\pi}{3} \frac{2\pi}{m_e} \frac{2}{m_2} \left( \frac{2\pi}{m_e} \right)^2 \frac{d\sigma}{d\Omega}.
\]
For elastic scattering, the electron's mass \( m_e \) is negligible, so \( E_i = |\mathbf{p}_i| \) and \( E_f = |\mathbf{p}_f| \). The four-momentum transfer \( q \) is defined as the difference between the final and initial four-momenta:
\[
q = P_f - P_i = (E_f - E_i)/c, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i
\]
The square of the four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is:
\[
Q^2 = q^2 = (P_f - P_i)^2 = (E_f - E_i)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i) \right)^2
\]
Substituting the expressions for \( P_i \) and \( P_f \):
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c} \right)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2
\]
Since the electron mass is negligible, \( E_i = |\mathbf{p}_i| \) and \( E_f = |\mathbf{p}_f| \). Substituting these:
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{|\mathbf{p}_f| - |\mathbf{p}_i|}{c} \right)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)^2
\]
This is the final expression for \( Q^2 \).",fluency,"# Task Description
