   - The hydrolysis of ATP is the reverse of the standard reaction for ATP synthesis:
     \[ \text{ATP} \rightarrow \text{ADP} + \text{Pi} \]
   - The standard free energy change for the hydrolysis reaction is:
     \[ \Delta G^\circ_{\text{hydrolysis}} = - \Delta G^\circ_{\text{ATP}} = 30.5 \, \text{kJ/mol} \]

3. **Effect of Temperature and Concentration**:
