","The presence of dark matter plays a significant role in the formation and evolution of black holes in the universe. Dark matter is a hypothetical form of matter that does not interact with electromagnetic radiation, making it invisible to telescopes. However, it is believed to make up about 27% of the total mass-energy content of the universe and its gravitational effects on visible matter are significant.

