2. **Velocity After Collision**:  
   The coefficient of restitution \( e = \frac{1}{3} \) is the ratio of the relative velocities of the two particles after and after impact. Since the wall is stationary, the relative velocity of the ball relative to the wall is \( v \cos \theta \).  
   The relative velocity of the ball after impact is \( e \times v \cos \theta = \frac{1}{3} v \cos \theta \).  
   The relative velocity of the wall relative to the ball after impact is \( v \cos \theta \).  
   The relative velocity of the ball relative to the wall after impact is \( v \cos \theta \).  

   The velocity of the ball after the collision is \( v' = v \cos \theta \).  

3. **Velocity Components**:  
   - Initial velocity: \( v_x = v \cos \theta \), \( v_y = v \sin \theta \)  
